00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:48.680
<v Tobias Wolff>There was a fern-choked gully behind the school. There were the stands by the football field, empty classrooms. She tasted of lipstick and cigarettes and candy. Which she opened her mouth to his, the first sensation was a shock of relief as the tightness melted in a rush from his neck and shoulders. And then, he was swaying with her, drinking that smoky sweetness, drinking forgetfulness of the schoolwork he had not done, the stammer he was developing, his mother dazed and pale, the room at the end of the hallway where his father lay gasping for the next breath like a trout dropped on the river bank.
<v Tobias Wolff>学校后面有一条长满蕨类植物的深沟。足球场边有看台，还有空旷的教室。她嘴里有口红、香烟和糖的味道。当她向他张开嘴时，第一感觉是一种如释重负的冲击，他脖子和肩膀的紧绷感瞬间消融。接着，他与她一起摇摆，饮下那烟熏般的甜蜜，饮下对他没完成功课、他正在形成的结巴、他那迷茫而苍白的母亲、以及他父亲躺在走廊尽头房间里像被扔在河岸上的鳟鱼一样喘息的遗忘。

00:19:48.680 --> 00:20:04.870
<v Tobias Wolff>He forgot to plan what to try next, where to touch, how hard to press. He stopped thinking ahead. There was no ahead, no before, and no after. He was itchy with thirst and deeply satisfied all at once.
<v Tobias Wolff>他忘了计划下一步该做什么，该摸哪里，该用力多大。他停止了预想。没有未来，没有过去，也没有将来。他口渴难耐，却又同时感到深深的满足。

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:32.400
<v Tobias Wolff>And Mary Claude was thirsty for him. He'd never have this happened before, a girl impatient for the taste of him, greedy for it. She did not like to break off. When he leaned away for a breath, she would close her fingers in his hair and pull him back to her. She sometimes said his name in a low, almost mocking way, and the sound of it whipped him around is if she'd yanked on a leash.
<v Tobias Wolff>而玛丽·克劳德也渴求着他。他从未见过这种情况，一个女孩迫不及待地想要他的味道，对此如饥似渴。她不喜欢中断。当他倾身喘气时，她会用手指抓紧他的头发，把他拉回身边。她有时会用一种低沉、近乎嘲弄的口吻叫他的名字，那声音鞭打着他，仿佛她拉紧了拴狗的链子。

00:20:32.400 --> 00:21:13.100
<v Tobias Wolff>Mary Claude some grew careless with their privacy. She didn't care who saw them or when. She'd command a kiss-- a profound kiss-- as she boarded her bus, or in the hallway, even on the street in town when her father let her go in for some shopping after school. Joe knew that it went beyond carelessness, that she was making a display of their appetite, perhaps especially of his appetite for her. He could see that she was proud of her claim on him, and this made him proud and brazen too. He didn't mind if people thought they were ridiculous, even a sort of joke, the two of them stitched together at the mouth, as his mother put it.
<v Tobias Wolff>玛丽·克劳德后来对他们的私密变得不那么在意了。她不在乎谁会看到，也不在乎什么时候。她在上校车时，或在走廊里，甚至在放学后她父亲让她进城购物时的街上，都会索要一个吻——一个深刻的吻。乔知道这不仅是粗心，她在炫耀他们的欲望，尤其是他对她的欲望。他能看出她为自己对他拥有的掌控力感到骄傲，这让他也感到自豪和大胆。他不介意别人觉得他们可笑，甚至把他们当笑话，正如他母亲所说，他们两个是嘴对嘴缝在一起的。

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:45.530
<v Tobias Wolff>Joe's mother had heard about them. She heard everything in the pharmacy. At first, she came at him aslant about it. Then she lost patience. Was this the time to be carrying on with some girl? Couldn't he sit with his father a while instead of mooning in his room and tying up the telephone? Would that be too much to ask? Joe knew he should care that he was giving his mother trouble, but nothing she said touched him. It wasn't out of concern for her that he ruined everything.
<v Tobias Wolff>乔的母亲听说过他们。她在药店里什么都能听到。起初，她侧面敲击地问过他。后来她失去了耐心。这是和某个女孩鬼混的时候吗？他能不能多陪陪他父亲，而不是在他房间里发呆和占用电话？这难道要求过分吗？乔知道他应该在意自己给母亲惹了麻烦，但她所说的一切都触动不了他。他弄砸一切并非出于对她的担忧。

00:21:45.530 --> 00:22:21.390
<v Tobias Wolff>He and Mary Claude were in the stands during a basketball game. She was bored. She wanted to leave, go outside. Joe kept putting her off. The game was close. She started to play with the hair at the nape of his neck. He liked the feeling, and almost surrendered to it, but something came over him, and he shrugged her hand off. He felt Mary Claude go still beside him. He knew she was looking at him, but he kept his eyes on the players, and even produced a shout when one of them goofed a pass.
<v Tobias Wolff>他和玛丽·克劳德在篮球比赛期间坐在看台上。她无聊了。她想离开，去外面。乔一直搪塞她。比赛正处于关键时刻。她开始玩弄他后颈的头发。他喜欢这种感觉，差点就屈服了，但某种情绪袭上心头，他耸肩甩开了她的手。他感觉到玛丽·克劳德在他身边静止了。他知道她在看着他，但他保持视线盯着球员，甚至在其中一人传球失误时还喊了一声。

00:22:21.390 --> 00:22:44.740
<v Tobias Wolff>Mary Claude slid her fingers back into his hair, tightened them, and began to turn his head toward hers. Without taking his eyes from the game, he gave a rough shake and pulled away. Mary Claude stood up, but waited there a moment. And though Joe knew he could still turn to her, even then, he did not.
<v Tobias Wolff>玛丽·克劳德将手指插回他的头发，用力抓紧，开始转动他的头使其转向自己。他不看比赛，粗暴地摇了摇头并甩开了她。玛丽·克劳德站起身，但在那里等了一会儿。尽管乔知道即使在那时他依然可以转向她，但他没有。

00:22:44.740 --> 00:23:12.840
<v Tobias Wolff>She made her way to the aisle. He watched her descend the steps and cross in front of the stands and leave the gym. The game had become meaningless to him, but he sat through the rest of it. His mouth was dry. His heart thudded as if it were hollow.
<v Tobias Wolff>她走向过道。他看着她走下台阶，从看台前穿过，离开了健身房。比赛对他来说已经变得毫无意义，但他还是坐着看完了剩下的部分。他嘴里发干。他的心脏砰砰作响，仿佛空空如也。

